  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (governmental funds cash basis; proprietary funds on an accrual basis with capital assets and depreciation). The government-wide Statement of Net Position is not in the trim (trim: Statement of Activities p1, governmental funds balance sheet p2, governmental revenues/expenditures p3, proprietary net position p4, proprietary revenues/expenses p5-6, cash flows p7-8, all-funds budgetary schedule p9, General Fund departments combining p10). Governmental roll-forward uses fund balance (beginning 569,785.42 + restatement 22,294.69 = 592,080.11 as restated; ending 550,234.80); beginning cash not printed. Certificates of deposit 43,948.22 are in ending_investments. Business-type from the proprietary statement Total column (ties to the Statement of Activities: expenses 952,615.25, charges 1,176,275.11, other receipts 12,785.56, investment earnings 12,399.15); prior period adjustment (34,327.09) recorded as business_type.restatement. Balance sheet combines the governmental funds balance sheet (Total Governmental Funds) and the proprietary statement of net position (Total); total_* are sums of the two printed totals. Detail: the all-funds budget schedule (p9) is not recorded (combined all-funds schedule); detail = General Fund departments combining schedule (p10) only (aligned with FY2024: no statement-column lines for the other governmental or proprietary funds, user rule 2026-10-28). Basis recorded as GAAP-style like FY2024 (fund-balance roll-forward; governmental_net_position from the Statement of Activities p1). ending_cash = Cash 927,634.28 + Cash held by County Treasurer 11,907.27 (as FY2024). Ambulance detail in health/welfare and Community Center / Community development in culture/recreation per the Statement of Activities (p1), as FY2024; the statement line General government still includes Ambulance as printed (p3). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
